    {
      "id": "query-attribute",
      "name": "QueryAttribute",
      "category": "tinyxml2",
      "signature": "QueryAttribute(Target, Name, Value)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "TINYXML2_LIB*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Name",
          "type": "char*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Value",
          "type": "Int*"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "XMLError",
      "docs": "Given an attribute name, QueryAttribute() returns\nXML_SUCCESS, XML_WRONG_ATTRIBUTE_TYPE if the conversion\ncan't be performed, or XML_NO_ATTRIBUTE if the attribute\ndoesn't exist. It is overloaded for the primitive types,\nand is a generally more convenient replacement of\nQueryIntAttribute() and related functions.\nIf successful, the result of the conversion\nwill be written to 'value'. If not successful, nothing will\nbe written to 'value'. This allows you to provide default\nvalue:\n@verbatim\nint value = 10;\nQueryAttribute( \"foo\", &value );\t\t// if \"foo\" isn't found, value will still be 10\n@endverbatim"
    },
